Model weights
-------------

The audio service's perceptual features use six Essentia models from the Music Technology
Group (https://essentia.upf.edu/models): msd-musicnn-1, discogs-effnet-bs64-1,
deam-msd-musicnn-2, danceability-msd-musicnn-1, mood_acoustic-discogs-effnet-1 and
voice_instrumental-msd-musicnn-1.

- Licence: CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/); the Music
  Technology Group offers a proprietary licence on request.
- The weights are neither in this repository nor in any image. services/audio/
  docker-entrypoint.sh downloads them when the container starts, into the /app/models volume,
  and services/audio/download_models.py checks each file's SHA-256.
- The non-commercial term binds any deployment that loads them. Without them
  (AUDIO_FETCH_MODELS=0) the service still measures tempo and key, and /health reports
  "degraded".


Evaluation reports
------------------

These files hold per-clip results derived from annotated datasets. They are under the
annotations' licences, not the code licence, and each report credits its datasets.

- evals/reports/audio-2026-10-25.md and evals/reports/audio-2026-10-25.json: Ballroom, GiantSteps
  Tempo and GiantSteps Key.
- evals/reports/audio-2026-10-29.md and evals/reports/audio-2026-10-29.json: Ballroom and
  GiantSteps Key.
- evals/audio/tests/fixtures/audio-schema4.json and audio-schema4.md: the first report's
  Ballroom and GiantSteps Key results, trimmed for a test.

The annotation licences:

- Ballroom (ISMIR 2004 tempo induction contest): CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, per mirdata 1.0.0; the
  dataset itself states no licence.
- GiantSteps Tempo: CC BY-SA 4.0, per mirdata 1.0.0; the annotation repository has no licence.
- GiantSteps Key, as GiantSteps+: CC BY-SA 4.0, stated in its Zenodo record
  (https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.1095691).

The audio of these datasets is commercial excerpts. It is fetched for evaluation only and is
never in this repository. evals/reports/audio-2026-10-30.* measures generated signals only and
is under the code licence.


Data sources
------------

The app reads these providers at run time. Their data stays under their terms. The recorded
answers kept for tests and replays (fixtures/, apps/api/src/sources/fixtures/ and
evals/agent/runs/) hold such data too, and are not under the code licence.

- MusicBrainz: recordings, works, releases and their relationships. Core data CC0.
- Cover Art Archive: release covers, shown with a credit. The images belong to their owners.
- Deezer: 30-second previews, the only audio the service measures, and their metadata.
- Spotify: search and track metadata only. Its previews are never analysed, since Spotify's
  terms restrict using its content for machine learning.
- Last.fm: tags, similar tracks and artists, artist information.
- Genius: song relationships (samples, interpolations, covers, remixes); no lyrics.
- ListenBrainz: similar artists (ListenBrainz Labs).
- SecondHandSongs: originals and covers.
- Discogs: release credits. Data provided by Discogs.
- Tavily: web search results, quoted as evidence. The pages belong to their publishers.

Cover art shown in the app, in recorded runs or in screenshots belongs to its owners.
